WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.460
<v Lecturer>Okay, so let's talk about AWS Organizations,</v>

2
00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:03.540
which is a way for you

3
00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:06.090
to manage multiple AWS accounts at once.

4
00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:07.590
So within Organizations,

5
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:11.220
we have, at the top, the root organizational unit,

6
00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.390
or OU,

7
00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:14.790
and it will contain our management account,

8
00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.230
which is the account that will be used

9
00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.330
for all administration purposes.

10
00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:22.350
Then within the root OU, you can have different OUs.

11
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:24.810
You can have an OU for your development environment,

12
00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:28.170
and this OU can have multiple member accounts.

13
00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:29.490
So you have to make a distinction

14
00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:30.599
between the management account

15
00:00:30.599 --> 00:00:32.010
that you use to manage all the other accounts

16
00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:33.300
and organizations.

17
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.410
And then the member accounts,

18
00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:36.210
which are just normal AWS accounts

19
00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.580
that are part of an organization.

20
00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.840
So we can have an OU for dev,

21
00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.400
we can have an OU for prod as well

22
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.140
with other member accounts.

23
00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.610
And we can have OU within OU.

24
00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:48.240
So it's very possible to have an HR OU within the prod OU,

25
00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.828
which is, by the way, within the root OU.

26
00:00:50.828 --> 00:00:52.950
So you can have HR or finance and so on.

27
00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:54.480
So once we have all these accounts,

28
00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:58.140
how does Organizations perform its administration?

29
00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.640
Well, there is a very special role

30
00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:00.840
you need to know about for the exam

31
00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.930
called the organization account access role.

32
00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.400
So when we have the organization

33
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:06.660
and the management account,

34
00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:09.180
if we happen to create a member account

35
00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:12.600
using an API from the Organization service,

36
00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:16.050
then, automatically, an IAM role within the member account

37
00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:17.130
is going to be created.

38
00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:18.570
And that IAM role is called

39
00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:21.300
the Organization Account Access Role.

40
00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.290
Now, the management account,

41
00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.750
when it needs to perform administrative duties

42
00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:26.460
onto the member account,

43
00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:28.770
will assume that administrative role

44
00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:30.930
using the AssumeRole API.

45
00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:34.260
So this IAM role grants full administrator permissions

46
00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.510
in the member account to the management account.

47
00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:40.380
And this is the magic of how AWS Organizations work.

48
00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:44.010
Now, this role is going to be used by the management account

49
00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:46.200
to perform admin task in the member account,

50
00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.330
for example, creating IAM users.

51
00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:50.460
This role can also be assumed by IAM users

52
00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:53.220
in the management account if they're authorized to do so.

53
00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:56.010
And, as I said, this role is automatically added

54
00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:57.570
to new member accounts created

55
00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:00.780
with the API of AWS Organizations.

56
00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:04.470
But in case you are inviting an account into an organization

57
00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:06.720
and that account already exists from out there,

58
00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:09.030
then you must manually create this role.

59
00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:11.280
Otherwise, things will not work.

60
00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:13.770
Now, we have an OU and multiple accounts.

61
00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:15.570
So we have multiple account strategy.

62
00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:18.810
And you can create accounts per department, per cost center,

63
00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:20.850
per environment, physical dev/test/prod.

64
00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:24.660
You can create them based on regulatory restrictions.

65
00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.480
You can get them for better resource isolation,

66
00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.670
for example, you wanna have one account per VPC,

67
00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:32.880
or you want to have separate per-account service limits,

68
00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:34.230
or you want to have a separate account

69
00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:35.850
for logging and so on.

70
00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:37.980
So you have, you know, different strategies to look at.

71
00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:39.480
For example, do you want multi accounts

72
00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:42.960
or one account with a multi VPC in it?

73
00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:44.970
And then of course you can share multiple accounts.

74
00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:46.260
So you need to have tagging standards

75
00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:47.940
for billing purposes, as we'll see this.

76
00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:49.920
And then some things we may want to do

77
00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.110
is to enable CloudTrail on all accounts

78
00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:54.150
and then send all the logs of CloudTrail

79
00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:57.750
into a central account that will have an Amazon S3 bucket,

80
00:02:57.750 --> 00:02:59.820
or also maybe aggregate

81
00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:01.710
all the CloudWatch logs within all accounts

82
00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:03.480
into a central logging account,

83
00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:06.540
or maybe create a central account for security.

84
00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:09.780
So these are just strategies. There's really no guideline.

85
00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:11.340
It's up to you and your architecture

86
00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:13.080
to decide what you want to do.

87
00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.420
So you have a business unit type of OU.

88
00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:16.950
So you have management account,

89
00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:19.500
then a OU per business unit,

90
00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:22.620
and then maybe multiple accounts within each business unit.

91
00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:24.480
You can also get, for example, a management account

92
00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:27.960
and then dev/test/prod types of OUs.

93
00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:30.810
And then you can also get project-based type of OUs.

94
00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.220
It's really up to you to decide,

95
00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:34.890
but this just gives you a few ideas.

96
00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:36.990
So there are two feature modes you need to know

97
00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:38.277
for AWS Organization.

98
00:03:38.277 --> 00:03:41.790
The first one is a consolidated billing feature.

99
00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:44.640
So this is going to aggregate billing across all accounts

100
00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.260
and gives you a single payment method

101
00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:48.780
directly from the management account.

102
00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:50.670
And the reason you do so is that you're going to get

103
00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:53.640
pricing benefits from the aggregated usage.

104
00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:55.920
You're going to get volume discounts for EC2,

105
00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:57.210
for Amazon S3, and so on

106
00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:00.090
because you are using more across all accounts.

107
00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:03.450
All the features are also going to be another feature mode

108
00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:04.530
for Organizations.

109
00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:06.210
So this, of course,

110
00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:08.610
includes the consolidated billing feature,

111
00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:11.580
but on top of it, it adds the SCP feature

112
00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:13.350
that we'll see in the next lecture.

113
00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:15.930
And in case you invite an account,

114
00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:18.480
it needs to approve enabling all features

115
00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.220
to be part of that mode.

116
00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:21.990
And then once you have the all features enabled,

117
00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:23.310
then we can use an SCP,

118
00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:25.500
so a service control policy,

119
00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:27.210
to prevent the member account

120
00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:29.310
from ever leaving the organization.

121
00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:31.560
And this is why the accounts that have been invited

122
00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:33.420
into an organization with all features

123
00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:36.300
must approve these features beforehand.

124
00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.040
And once you have enabled all features,

125
00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:40.620
you cannot go back to using Organizations

126
00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:43.200
only to consolidate billing.

127
00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:44.033
Okay.

128
00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:46.770
So talking about what is shared and savings,

129
00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:49.620
we have reserved instances in Organizations.

130
00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:51.120
So for billing purposes,

131
00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:54.000
the consolidated billing feature of AWS Organizations

132
00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.850
will treat all the accounts as one account that we know.

133
00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:58.740
That means that all the accounts in the organization

134
00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:02.730
will receive the hourly cost benefit of a reserved instance

135
00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:04.920
that is purchased by any other account.

136
00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:06.240
So that means that it will give you

137
00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:08.010
the maximum amount of saving,

138
00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:09.300
even if a specific account

139
00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:12.390
is not using that reserve instance but another is.

140
00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:14.970
So the payer accounts of an organization,

141
00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:16.110
so the management account,

142
00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:19.290
can turn off the RI, reserve instance sharing,

143
00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:21.000
or savings plan discount sharing,

144
00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:23.100
for any account including VPR accounts.

145
00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:25.567
So it's possible for you to disable it and say,

146
00:05:25.567 --> 00:05:27.420
"Well, this RI or this savings plan

147
00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:30.420
only belongs to that specific account."

148
00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:32.850
That means that in that case,

149
00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:35.400
then the reserve instances and savings plan discounts

150
00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.230
will not be shared across accounts

151
00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:39.060
that have this turned off.

152
00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:43.020
And then, on the opposite side, for a reserved instance

153
00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:46.800
or a savings plan to be shared across two accounts,

154
00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:50.160
then both these accounts must have sharing turned on, okay?

155
00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:53.580
So this is a little thing that the exam can test you on.

156
00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:54.900
You need to also know the process

157
00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:57.360
to move accounts between two organizations.

158
00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:59.310
So let's say we want to move a member account

159
00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:01.590
from an old to a new organization.

160
00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:04.530
First, we just send an invite to the member account,

161
00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.720
and then we're going to accept the invite

162
00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.070
from the member account.

163
00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:09.240
It's as simple as that.

164
00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:11.430
Before, we had to remove the member account

165
00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:12.690
from the previous organization,

166
00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:13.523
but now we don't.

167
00:06:13.523 --> 00:06:15.540
We just send an invite and it can be moved over

168
00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:17.370
across two organizations.

169
00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:18.203
All right.

170
00:06:18.203 --> 00:06:19.036
So that's it for this lecture.

171
00:06:19.036 --> 00:06:20.010
I hope you liked it,

172
00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:21.960
and I will see you in the next lecture.

